@*
    DrawerShell — reusable right slide-in drawer chrome (overlay + panel + header + body + footer).

    Presentation only. It owns the surface and nothing entity-specific: the dimmed overlay, the
    ~620px right panel (full-width sheet at ≤768px), the header row with a close button, the
    scrollable body, an optional pinned footer, and the three ways to dismiss (close button, overlay
    click, Escape). Visual design is locked in SPEC/mockups/comp-c-review-09-detail-surfaces.html —
    do not restyle here. Any entity/URL-specific logic stays in the host component.

    On any dismiss the shell simply raises OnClose; the host decides whether to actually close (e.g.
    to block dismissal mid-save). Extracted from IdeaDrawer for reuse across the admin List+Drawer
    conversions (Organizations, Users, Statuses, Idea Types, Custom Fields).

    Public API
      IsOpen           bool             When false the shell renders nothing.
      OnClose          EventCallback    Raised on close button, overlay click, or Escape.
      Title            string?          Heading text; also the aria-labelledby target.
      Eyebrow          string?          Small uppercase kicker above the title.
      Meta             string?          Small secondary line below the title.
      HeaderContent    RenderFragment?  Optional; replaces the Eyebrow/Title/Meta block inside the header.
      SubHeaderContent RenderFragment?  Optional; sits between header and the scrollable body (e.g. inline
                                        flash/status), so it is not scrolled away with the body.
      ChildContent     RenderFragment?  The scrollable body.
      FooterContent    RenderFragment?  Optional pinned action bar; the footer element is omitted when null.

    Usage
      <DrawerShell IsOpen="@(_selectedId is not null)" OnClose="Close"
                   Eyebrow="Organization" Title="@_name" Meta="@_meta">
          <ChildContent>...detail / edit form...</ChildContent>
          <FooterContent>
              <button class="btn" @onclick="Close">Cancel</button>
              <button class="btn primary" @onclick="Save">Save</button>
          </FooterContent>
      </DrawerShell>
*@

@if (IsOpen)
{
    <div class="surface-backdrop open" @onclick="OnClose"></div>
    <aside class="drawer open" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
           aria-labelledby="@(Title is not null ? _titleId : null)"
           tabindex="-1" @onkeydown="OnKeyDown">
        <header class="surface-head">
            <div class="grow">
                @if (HeaderContent is not null)
                {
                    @HeaderContent
                }
                else
                {
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Eyebrow))
                    {
                        <div class="eyebrow">@Eyebrow</div>
                    }
                    <h2 id="@_titleId">@Title</h2>
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Meta))
                    {
                        <div class="meta">@Meta</div>
                    }
                }
            </div>
            <button class="iconbtn" @onclick="OnClose" aria-label="Close">×</button>
        </header>

        @if (SubHeaderContent is not null)
        {
            @SubHeaderContent
        }

        <div class="surface-body">
            @ChildContent
        </div>

        @if (FooterContent is not null)
        {
            <footer class="surface-foot">@FooterContent</footer>
        }
    </aside>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool IsOpen { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Eyebrow { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Meta { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? HeaderContent { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? SubHeaderContent { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? FooterContent { get; set; }

    // Stable per-instance id so the panel's aria-labelledby resolves without colliding across instances.
    private readonly string _titleId = $"drawer-title-{Guid.NewGuid():N}";

    private async Task OnKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e.Key == "Escape")
        {
            await OnClose.InvokeAsync();
        }
    }
}
